From 7b90a0c30c1b55af7cb6abbdbf5e3d48553a5a37 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 6 Jul 2026 06:31:34 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?feat(cli):=20orientation=20front=20door=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=E2=80=94=20one-glance=20status,=20per-command=20help,=20bare-f?=
 =?UTF-8?q?orge=20orient?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Make both users and agents grasp "you are here / what next / why" without
learning all of forge.

A. Canonical stage model in the status surface: workflow-profiles.js now lists
   only the 6 canonical stages under `stages` and moves `/status` to a new
   `utilities` key (a status utility is not a numbered stage). The one-glance
   view renders "Stage N of M — Label (classification workflow)" from the
   per-classification path in lib/workflow/stages.js, so non-stages never get a
   number.

B. Zero-arg `forge status` is a top-down one-glance view: You are here →
   Context (one line) → Your work → newcomer footer. The dead-end null branch
   is replaced with a STATE-AWARE fallback (claim a ready issue, else /plan).
   A one-line "Why" is derived from the last completed stage. Blocked/Stale/
   Recent-Completions move behind `--full`. The Run-now/Next-after-this lines
   are extracted into one shared presenter helper that status.js delegates to.

C. Bare `forge` in an INITIALIZED project renders the same read-only view
   instead of running the mutating minimal install (still falls to setup when
   uninitialized).

D. `forge <cmd> --help` renders that command's usage/description/flags instead
   of the global setup banner; bare `forge --help` keeps the banner.

E. node:sqlite's require-time ExperimentalWarning is suppressed at its source
   (wrap process.emitWarning only around the require, match /SQLite/, restore
   immediately) — no --no-warnings re-exec.

Kernel refs: 2416b136, 4d6f5d68, 4b82b31c, a9bbd065.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
